     1                                  ; E2 (day2 round 2) CF = DET2 + merge-kill via the worker's LAST instruction: call far [bx] -> call far [00300h] (FF 1E 00 03),
     2                                  ; with one private pointer cell 0300h for A, B and captured zombies (was 2C0h / 280h). Port of D8 MC2's idea onto DET2 without
     3                                  ; moving any worker byte: MC2's mov di,[0300h] is 2 bytes longer and shifts stosw/dec di/call far by 2 bytes; on DET2's 42h
     4                                  ; lattice the worker's call far [bx] sits exactly on the V6-family anchor (in-page 52h, our anchor + 10h), where a V6 anchor
     5                                  ; write FF 1F is byte-identical; MC2 put stosw/dec di there instead (DETMC lost in every V6-family cohort, confirm field).
     6                                  ; Here bytes anchor+1..anchor+17 are identical to DET2 (FF at +16, 1E at +17), so that coincidence is kept; a V6 FF 1F write
     7                                  ; at +16 turns our call far [0300h] into call far [bx] = the same cell for us. A foreign V6/zchain-family process that runs
     8                                  ; one of our worker copies reads its own private [0300h] = 0 and far-calls 0000:0000 (outside the arena) -> memory exception.
     9                                  ; Template copy stays mov cx,10 (20 bytes: worker 19 + one CC), so all timings are DET2's. Cost: stale copies no longer carry
    10                                  ; the FF 1F CC CC searcher decoy at +16 (they carry FF 1E 00 03).
    11                                  ; Good_Test V6 is friend-provided code; DET2 by agent2 day2 D4; MC idea by D8; CF edits by agent2 day2 E2.
    12                                  ; D4 DET2: DET with B's [5D13h]/[0CC13h] writes back at instr 4/5 (rev1 rounds). DET's instr-3 [0CC13h]
    13                                  ; write tied with the zchain/zrl03/ah02 A write (instr 3) and lost the p0f13 hook half the time (screen n6sgd).
    14                                  ; D4 DET (day2, base rev1 KPHL): adaptive whole-team lattice. If a V6-family team is present (its B writes
    15                                  ; [4A17h] at instr 3; no other team in our fields writes that cell), every stream of ours (A, B, captured zombies)
    16                                  ; uses FAR_SEG 0FFAh = lattice 42h (10h below the V6-family 52h lattice, measured +0.28/+0.24 on leader2/3 cohorts
    17                                  ; in D4 W42 screen 0b3hc); otherwise FAR_SEG 0FFBh = 52h as in rev1 (W42's plain 2025/strong cost avoided).
    18                                  ; Detection: our B now writes [4A17h] late (instr 7), so at A's instr 5 and B's instr 5 the cell is still CCCCh
    19                                  ; unless a V6-family B wrote it at instr 3. A keeps the bit in BP; B patches the low byte of its own phoenix
    20                                  ; 'or dx,0FFBh' immediate (dec -> 0FAh) before any captured zombie can reach phoenix_init.
    21                                  ; Good_Test V6 is friend-provided code (see the provenance comments below); DET edits by agent2 day2 role D4.
    22                                  ; COMBINE (night combination coordinator, 2026-10-04, base rev0): KPHL = KP + h34 (B099 KPH_B) + locpatA (B092 KL_A). A = KL_A unchanged; B = B099 KPH_B.
    23                                  ; Good_Test V6 is friend-provided code; V6nohunt and all night edits by agent2 roles (see FINDINGS.md).
    24                                  bits 16
    25                                  
    26                                  ; B092 KL (warrior A): A031 K (E1 INT86 decoy block + A022 SD template edits) combined with the
    27                                  ; domain-2 defense A038 locpatA (B082 location start DI = 15*[1243h] + A038 window F2 81 C3 E1 -> FF 26 17 4A).
    28                                  ; Provenance: Good_Test V6 warrior 1 is friend-provided code (reconstructed source in
    29                                  ; study-notes/good-test-v6/source/); V6nohunt = agent2 edit (removed [7A00h] patch); E1/SD/locA2/locpatA are
    30                                  ; agent2 night edits (A031, A022, B082, A038); this merge = agent2 night role B092.
    31                                  ; Turn budget: locpatA startup (INT87 at instr 11) + E1 block (4 instr) + band math with a memory divisor
    32                                  ; (div/mul word [kq] instead of mov cx,3C00h; div cx; mul cx: same AX, one instruction fewer) + add si;
    33                                  ; phoenix_init still starts at turn 22 (as in rev0, K and locpatA). Data moved to the end (no jmp needed).
    34                                  ; B = A031 K_B (A026 Z1 + SD) unchanged.
